{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1415095-a-special-arcane-experience-needed-to-raise-magic","id":1415095,"title":"A special Arcane Experience needed to raise magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-22T11:35:02-07:00","id":1415095,"title":"A special Arcane Experience needed to raise magic","content":"So I\u2019m listening to the Mage podcast and I got to thinking how I like Arcane Experience in Awakening and Solar experience in Exalted. I remember years ago I was pondering what if Ascension had it and an author pointed out it would work but you need to change what qualifies for gaining experience because awakening is about understanding the Supernal truth while Ascension is about subjective truth. I did a similar thing with my 1st ed Scion house rules.<br /> <br /> But so you don\u2019t have to invest all your concentration on Arete or spheres at the expense of everything else what if this Arcane Exp is the only way to raise arete and maybe spheres as well, though maybe you just have spheres need half the exp from your Arcane Exp.<br /> <br /> In this way I can include the wonderful seasonal Exp systems where spending a season studying/rearching can net you Arcane Exp. This has the benefit of both controlling more the magical Potence/growth of the group while also not having them worry about investing only in magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T13:18:29-07:00","id":1415107,"title":"","content":"Broadly, yeah it's been discussed before to bring something like Awakening's Arcane Experience to Ascension. That Ascension's EXP as is encourages players to bank all of their EXP towards Arete and Sphere rankings...while forgetting to devote it to silly things like Attributes and Abilities. On top of the EXP costs for Arete and Sphere being ridiculously high.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T18:31:48-07:00","id":1415143,"title":"","content":"I'm in favor of the idea. That said, basing it on study doesn't really work all that well for many Foci (or Paradigms, if you prefer the earlier editions' terminology). It works quite well for High Ritualists in general and Hermetics in particular (which shouldn't be surprising, seeing as how Awakening's magic system is essentially Hermetic in nature; you could view Awakening as an example of what might happen if the Order of Hermes were to win the Ascension War); but it doesn't work so well for, say, a witch, a shaman, or a priest. <br /> <br /> Taking the priest as an example, his Arete and Spheres should most readily improve as he seems to serve the Divine \u2014 which <i>can</i> take the form of study (of the sacred scriptures), but is ultimately less about gaining knowledge per se and more about attuning oneself to the will of whatever higher power you serve. <br /> <br /> More generally, this means of earning special experience out to be reflective of just what you think Arete <i>is</i>: if you want, this could be used to being an element of Dark Ages: Mage into modern Ascension, by using the Foundations as a sort of guideline for different ways that one might conceive of Arete, and build the means of earning Arcane Experience around that. Mind you, I'm thinking in terms of using the Foundations as a source of inspiration, not as a straitjacket: if you have an idea for what sorts of activities would be appropriate for your Focus and none of the Foundations cover it, disregard them and go with that activity instead \u2014 as long as the Storyteller approves, of course. <br /> <br /> As well, <b>Ascension</b> has the Avatar, which exists both to empower the mage and to guide him on his path to Ascension. That sounds <i>exactly</i> like the sort of thing that would be a source for an \u201cArcane Experience\u201d analog. These Avatars have four Essences, which could also be used to suggest ways that special experience could be earned. <br /> <br /> So that's what I'd do: I'd let Arcane Experience be earned in two ways, the first being a paradigm-specific activity roughly analogous to Hermetic study of supernatural mysteries, using DAMage's Foundations as a starting point for determining what sorts of activities might be appropriate; and the second being significant action that's in accordance with your Avatar's Essence. <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> In terms of <i>spending</i> this special experience, it should definitely be able to be spent on Arete and Spheres; but I'd also consider the possibility of letting it be spent on suitable Backgrounds (Avatar comes to mind), or even Abilities that are associated with your Practice. If you allow Merits in your game, Arcane Experience might also be able to purchase some of those, using your Focus and/or Avatar Essence as a guideline as to which ones might be appropriate.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> EDIT: maybe instead of using the Foundations as a source of inspiration, consider using the Approaches from <b>Mage Made Easy</b> instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-22-2020, 09:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T19:17:41-07:00","id":1415149,"title":"","content":"In practical experience playing Awakening 2e (pun not intended, but worth it), Arcane XP doesn't actually have a major impact on people spending a lot of their XP on Arcana and Gnosis (and so on since Awakening has more magical things to buy). Something that Awakening and Exalted both do is make sure there are things you can and can't spend Arcane/Solar XP on. There's also things like Awakening not putting as much emphasis on combining Arcana as Ascension does on combining Spheres for basic to intermediary effects.<br /> <br /> If all you do is add more XP to spend on Spheres and Arete... people will just buy those faster instead of having more reason to invest in other traits.<br /> <br /> When it comes to gaining Arcane XP... copy Awakening as much as possible: you get Arcane XP for actually doing magical stuff that matters, not sitting around studying.<br /> <br /> You get Arcane Beats in Awakening from:<br /> <br /> Making significant progress towards/resolving Obsessions<br /> Resolving Conditions that came from spell-casting<br /> Risking Wisdom<br /> Being tutored by your Legacy mentor, or tutoring your own students<br /> Encountering a novel supernatural phenomenon for the first time<br /> <br /> The tutoring one is the only that's even close to sitting around studying (and even then it's only as academic as the Legacy is). Awakening isn't &quot;What would Ascension look like if the Hermetics won.&quot; It's, &quot;What would it look like if Gnosticism won,&quot; because Gnosticism promotes mystic insight through active experience with the Divine rather than something you can obtain by simply doing what orthodox norms tell you to do.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T23:28:18-07:00","id":1415166,"title":"","content":"I consider practical experience as being included with studying. Even witches and shamans study but their study took different forms. Communion with the divine I consider study just as much as meditating under the bhodi tree. I\u2019m using study in broad terms. Notice I said study/research that includes discovering the properties of the local wildlife and herbs as well as learning sacred songs or just listening to the spirits.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m torn, as I like this as way to free up Exp as Arete would essentially be more akin to the renown of werewolf, and if you had it dedicated to just Arete it would be different compared to dedicating it to all magical traits. Being able to spend it on other magical traits could represent a sort of release valve as Exp builds up, you won\u2019t necessarily grow more enlightened as you explore methods of power and ability, which I guess is what Mage had in mind with the idea Archmages more often get sidetracked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T10:28:03-07:00","id":1415204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1415095-a-special-arcane-experience-needed-to-raise-magic?p=1415166#post1415166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Communion with the divine I consider study just as much as meditating under the bhodi tree. I\u2019m using study in broad terms. Notice I said study/research that includes discovering the properties of the local wildlife and herbs as well as learning sacred songs or just listening to the spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would rather interpret Dataweaver's servitude to the divine as much more than mere communion. For instance, building a temple it's considered great prestige, and in some Buddhist sects that has a correlation with your spiritual advancement. With christians I imagine that it would be similar, with how much missionaries matter in the folklore.<br /> <br /> I stand by the the idea of allowing this kind of activities it's on magical XP too. If we're making the comparison with Renown, this would make it even more akin to Renown because you're gaining it by following the precepts of your supernatural &quot;tribe&quot;, so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T10:43:25-07:00","id":1415208,"title":"","content":"I pretty much use the Library background to give study points for study. However, when characters do learn a great deal about magic from ways other than hitting the books, they can gain study points in Arete or Spheres. I make Arete much harder to earn study points in--characters really need to work to gain insight into reality.<br /> <br /> Perhaps someone should write up a 'study experience points for Arete and Spheres' work for the Storyteller's Vault.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T13:22:20-07:00","id":1415317,"title":"","content":"Exactly. Arcane Experience should <i>not</i> be \u201cstudy points\u201d, and should not reflect hitting the books or the like, with the possible exception of technomantic approaches such as are found in the Technocracy. If you have a mystical Focus, that should include some sort of mystical experience \u2014 something that's most blatantly expressed by the Cult of Ecstasy, but which every mystic should have in one way or another. <br /> <br /> And yes, I could see that mystical experience (as in, an event that the mage goes through) leading to a special kind of experience points suitable for Arete, Spheres, and other mystical traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T09:13:48-07:00","id":1417154,"title":"","content":"See one of my big issues is I want magic to take time to master. I want downtime between stories and including the idea that it takes years to raise up higher mastery.<br /> <br /> So one of the big points I want for Arcane Experience is time is a part of it, ignore the study aspect it represents time cultivating.<br /> <br /> But you still need some degree of knowledge to raise your spheres, not like you level up with pushups and you learn new secrets of fundamental forces. Sister Bernadette was illiterate but she spent time mastering Magic as music, that included practice and experience and learning certain knowledges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T10:00:36-07:00","id":1417162,"title":"","content":"To reiterate then:<br /> <br /> If you want to slow down how long magic takes to master, giving the players more XP in the from of special XP that's only good for mastering magic has the opposite effect.<br /> <br /> It feels like you'd be better served looking towards things like the Dark Ages Revised Maturation Points system. While it has some serious flaws in implementation, if you can only raise Arete and most Spheres (or more Spheres above a certain level like Arete/2 rounded up) with a cleaned up Maturation Point system you shunt most magic mastery into extended downtime activity. You could even incentivize spending XP on traits directly relevant to the PCs' Focus with increase Maturation Points.<br /> <br /> That would be flexible enough to avoid everything being &quot;studying&quot; but still creates extended downtimes as something important enough STs are going to use them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T13:01:53-07:00","id":1417196,"title":"","content":"Using the times to learn a sphere in the Bitter Road would be a good start. Those times presume some regular practice and study and are built along the Library and Mentor backgrounds as a way to learn more quickly. See page 73. . .<br /> <br /> If you give targeted experience, as Heavy Arms has said, it tends to let PCs buy that up more quickly than the base Mage assumption that requires all the experience be spent on a pool of everything. That's why I tend to give study points for studying and new discoveries of things other than Arete or Sphere study points. I know the players will want power and Arete and Spheres are quite powerful. To reflect mages as learned beings with above-average mental capabilities, they tend to get some study points in the main and secondary abilities.<br /> <br /> Though other methods may work, the Sphere study times, especially if you allow time in the campaign to progress as fitting the story rather than a 'we play a session every X days so the same amount of time can go by in game' timeframe. Because while roleplaying some of the magical learning may be fun, not all players enjoy spending two hours or more on obscure philosophical topics in game.<br /> <br /> Just be upfront with those house rules and be fair and the more reasonable players should enjoy it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}